IMPORT prelude

-- Government Contracts Act 1966 (Singapore) -- who may sign a Government contract made in Singapore (s 2), contracts made
-- outside Singapore (s 3), when a contract binds the Government at all (s 4), when the officer who made it can be sued
-- personally (s 5), and who signs grants and leases of State land (s 6). The whole Act is six sections; all are covered except
-- the short title (s 1) and the saving in s 6(2).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GCA1966.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; SSO
-- describes it as the current version as at 1 October 2026. The latest amendment annotated in the body is [5/2018] (s 2(3),
-- the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, in force 1 April 2018).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0115 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. A business contracting with a Ministry meets it as: will this contract bind the Government, and
-- if not, can I sue the officer I dealt with?
--
-- Not encoded: what "in accordance with ... the Constitution" requires (taken as a given fact); the general law of agency and
-- of ostensible authority, which the Act does not mention; the content of any Minister for Finance authorisation (its limit is
-- taken as a given number); s 6(2) (the Act does not affect written law on use or occupation of State land); and whether s 2
-- also applies to a grant or lease that s 6(1) governs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Government Contracts Act 1966 -- contracts`

DECLARE Signer IS ONE OF
    `a Minister`
    `a public officer`
    `a seconded statutory body employee`
    `an unseconded statutory body employee`
    `a private agent`

DECLARE Authorisation IS ONE OF
    `no written authorisation`
    `special written authorisation`
    `general written authorisation`

DECLARE Contract HAS
    `made after 15 March 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reduced to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the name of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signer` IS A Signer
    `authorisation by the Minister for Finance` IS AN Authorisation
    `value` IS A NUMBER
    `general authorisation limit` IS A NUMBER
    `within the jurisdiction of the Singapore courts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in accordance with the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2 -- contracts made in Singapore`

-- s 2(1): "All contracts made in Singapore for or on behalf of the Government shall, if reduced to writing, be made in the name
-- of the Government and may be signed by a Minister or by any public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister for
-- Finance, either specially in any particular case, or generally for all contracts below a certain value in his Ministry or
-- department."
-- s 2(3): "an individual who is an employee of a statutory body under a secondment arrangement making available temporarily to
-- the Government the service of the individual is deemed to be a public officer during that secondment." [5/2018]
--
-- A general authorisation covers contracts "below" a value: a contract AT the limit is outside it. The Act sets no figure.
GIVEN `the signer` IS A Signer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signer counts as a public officer` IF
    CONSIDER `the signer`
    WHEN `a public officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a seconded statutory body employee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signer is authorised under section 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`'s `signer`
    WHEN `a Minister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
            `the signer counts as a public officer` (`the contract`'s `signer`)
        AND CONSIDER `the contract`'s `authorisation by the Minister for Finance`
            WHEN `special written authorisation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `general written authorisation` THEN `the contract`'s `value` LESS THAN `the contract`'s `general authorisation limit`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2(2): "it shall be sufficient for the Minister for Finance to name the office held by such public officer and the Minister
-- MAY cause the authorisation to be published in the Gazette." Gazetting is optional; naming the office is enough.
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `names the individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `names the office` IS A BOOLEAN, `gazetted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authorisation identifies the officer sufficiently` IF
    `in writing` AND (`names the individual` OR `names the office`)

§§ `3 -- contracts made outside Singapore`

-- s 3: "All contracts made outside Singapore for or on behalf of the Government by a person either generally or specially
-- authorised in writing in that behalf by the Minister for Finance shall, so far as they come within the jurisdiction of the
-- courts in Singapore, be deemed to be Government contracts."
--
-- s 3 names "a person", not a public officer, and sets no value limit on a general authorisation. Nor does it mention a
-- Minister: a Minister signing abroad without the Minister for Finance's written authorisation is not within s 3.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is deemed a Government contract under section 3` IF
        (NOT `the contract`'s `made in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT (`the contract`'s `authorisation by the Minister for Finance` EQUALS `no written authorisation`))
    AND `the contract`'s `within the jurisdiction of the Singapore courts`

§§ `4 -- no other contracts bind the Government`

-- s 4: "No contracts, made after 15 March 1967, shall be binding upon the Government, unless entered into in accordance with this
-- Act and the Constitution."
--
-- INFERENCE (the text does not say this): a contract made in Singapore that is NOT reduced to writing is "in accordance with
-- this Act", because s 2 lays down form only "if reduced to writing". And a contract made outside Singapore is in accordance
-- with the Act only if made by a person the Minister for Finance authorised in writing, because s 3 is the only route the Act
-- gives for such contracts.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is in accordance with this Act` IF
    IF `the contract`'s `made in Singapore`
    THEN IF `the contract`'s `reduced to writing`
         THEN `the contract`'s `made in the name of the Government` AND `the signer is authorised under section 2` `the contract`
         ELSE TRUE
    ELSE NOT (`the contract`'s `authorisation by the Minister for Finance` EQUALS `no written authorisation`)

-- A contract made on or before 15 March 1967 is outside s 4: the Act neither bars nor validates it.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 bars the contract from binding the Government` IF
        `the contract`'s `made after 15 March 1967`
    AND NOT (`the contract is in accordance with this Act` `the contract` AND `the contract`'s `in accordance with the Constitution`)

§§ `5 -- personal liability of the public officer`

-- s 5: "No public officer shall be liable to be sued personally upon any contract which he makes in that capacity; but a public
-- officer shall be personally liable when he expressly pledges his personal credit or where he contracts otherwise than as the
-- agent of the Government."
--
-- The bar covers only contracts made "in that capacity". Outside it, s 5 says nothing, and the general law (not encoded)
-- decides; this rule answers only whether s 5 shields the officer.
GIVEN `made in the capacity of a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `expressly pledged personal credit` IS A BOOLEAN, `contracted as agent of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 shields the officer from being sued personally` IF
        `made in the capacity of a public officer`
    AND (NOT `expressly pledged personal credit`)
    AND `contracted as agent of the Government`

GIVEN `made in the capacity of a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `expressly pledged personal credit` IS A BOOLEAN, `contracted as agent of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 makes the officer personally liable` IF
    `expressly pledged personal credit` OR (NOT `contracted as agent of the Government`)

§§ `6 -- grants and leases of State land`

-- s 6(1): "Grants and leases of State lands and leases made under the Foreshores Act 1920 shall be signed by a Collector of Land
-- Revenue." Not a Minister, and not an officer authorised under s 2.
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `a grant of State land`
    `a lease of State land`
    `a lease under the Foreshores Act 1920`
    `a supply contract`

DECLARE LandSigner IS ONE OF
    `a Collector of Land Revenue`
    `the Minister for Law`
    `an officer authorised by the Minister for Finance`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 governs the signature` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `a supply contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the land signer` IS A LandSigner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature meets section 6` IF
        (NOT `section 6 governs the signature` `the instrument`)
    OR  `the land signer` EQUALS `a Collector of Land Revenue`
